            <ArticleTitle>Fungus ball in concha bullosa: an unusual cause of retro-orbital pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e138-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SCS.0000000000000472</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fungus ball in the concha bullosa is an extremely rare disease. We described a case of the fungus ball in the concha bullosa in a 22-year-old woman. Preoperative diagnosis was based on nasal endoscopy and computed tomography scanning. The patient was endoscopically operated on. The examination of the removed material was reported as fungal infection. This case was found worth writing because of the location of the concha bullosa and its rare occurrence in this location.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
